cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use mdz in your research, please cite it using these metadata."
type: software
title: "mdz: molecular dynamics trajectory compression with fast random access"
abstract: >-
  mdz compresses molecular dynamics trajectories (positions, velocities,
  forces and per-frame data) using inter-frame prediction, adaptive
  quantization and zstd, in groups of frames that are individually indexed
  for fast random access. It provides a C++ library, a command-line tool,
  Python bindings, a C API and a LAMMPS dump style.
authors:
  - family-names: Spackman
    given-names: Peter
    email: peterspackman@fastmail.com
repository-code: "https://github.com/peterspackman/mdz"
url: "https://github.com/peterspackman/mdz"
license: MIT
version: 0.4.0
keywords:
  - molecular dynamics
  - trajectory
  - compression
  - random access
